  "notes": "Source: Agora University 2025-2026 Catalog (official PDF, agora.edu; catalog revised 04/2/26), Section 43.2.3 Bachelor of Arts in Theology degree completion: 28 core courses x 3 credits = 84 credits (all 28 course titles hand-transcribed 2026-09-30). IMPORTANT CATALOG ARITHMETIC NOTE: the catalog requires 120 credits for the bachelor's degree (13.1), but the BAT core alone totals 84 credits and section 12.9.1.1 requires 42 semester units of general education for BAT transfer students - 84 + 42 = 126 exceeds the 120-credit degree total by 6 credits. This plan models the full 84-credit core plus 36 credits (six 6-unit) of general-education transfer slots = 120 credits, the degree requirement. The 7th gen-ed area (Civics, 6 units) is omitted from the model pending registrar clarification; total_credits equals the recomputed sum of modeled courses. Earlier institutional disclosures referenced BAT tracks in Arabic (BATE/BATA); the 2025-26 catalog contains only one BAT curriculum. Agora University is a fully online institution; the catalog gives no fixed semester map, so this plan models a self-paced 8-term sequence a degree-completion student could follow. All courses are 3-credit units per the catalog. Degree-completion students must complete at least 30% of the 120 credits at Agora; up to 70% may transfer.",
